Two faults that **mask** each other — for example two coupling faults on the same victim, one forcing it to 1 and the other back to 0. A test that triggers both before reading the victim sees the correct value.

Tests for linked faults order their operations so that every fault is read **before** the second one can undo it:

- **March A** (15N) and **March B** (17N) — linked idempotent coupling and transition faults;
- **March LR** (14N) — linked faults that are realistic in real layouts;
- **March SL** (41N) — all static linked faults.
